@UserManagementAPI_HostAddress = http://localhost:5024

### UserManagementAPI — CRUD + Basic auth tests
#
# Notes:
# - The API protects /users endpoints with a simple Basic auth middleware.
# - Example credentials included below (for local testing):
#     - admin:password  (Base64: YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=)
#     - user:secret     (Base64: dXNlcjpzZWNyZXQ=)
# - If you're using the VS Code REST Client extension, run the requests in order.

### 1) List users (no auth) — expect 401 Unauthorized
GET http://localhost:5000/users
Accept: application/json

### 2) List users (with Basic auth) — expect 200 OK
GET http://localhost:5000/users
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=
Accept: application/json

### 3) Create a user (authenticated) — expect 201 Created
POST http://localhost:5000/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=

{
	"firstName": "Sam",
	"lastName": "Lee",
	"age": 28
}

# Note: copy the "id" value from the Create response JSON and set it into the
# variable `createdId` below (replace the placeholder) before running the
# subsequent requests.

> {%
// Extract the created user's id from the POST response and store it as a global variable
// This handler runs in the REST Client extension. After running the Create request
// subsequent requests can use {{createdId}}.
client.global.set("createdId", JSON.parse(responseBody).id);
%}

### 4) Get the created user by id (authenticated)
GET http://localhost:5000/users/{{createdId}}
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=
Accept: application/json

### 5) Update the created user (authenticated) — expect 204 No Content
PUT http://localhost:5000/users/{{createdId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=

{
	"firstName": "Samantha",
	"lastName": "Lee",
	"age": 29
}

### 6) Delete the created user (authenticated) — expect 204 No Content
DELETE http://localhost:5000/users/{{createdId}}
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### 7) Verify deletion — Get should return 404 Not Found
GET http://localhost:5000/users/{{createdId}}
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQ=
Accept: application/json
